div.verse:
Pilate replied, How can he do this by wicked methods? They answered, He is a conjurer, and casts out devils by the prince of the devils; 
          Matt. vi. 24, and xi. 5.
          Matt. iv. 34, and xii. 24, &c. and so all things become subject to him.

Thus Moses, when he was sent by God into Egypt, wrought the miracles which God commanded him, before Pharaoh king of Egypt; and though the magicians of that country, Jannes and Jambres, 
          These are mentioned also as the names of the magicians, 2 Tim. iii. 8. wrought by their magic the same miracles which Moses did, yet they could not work all which he did; 
          Exod. viii. 18, &c.

That  
          Matt. xxviii. 11, 12, &c. while they were guarding the sepulchre of Jesus, there was an earthquake; and we saw an angel of God roll away the stone of the sepulchre and  
          Matt. xxviii. 1, 2, &c. sit upon it;
